## 1. Commands produce events
   concept: a command loads the stream, folds it into state, validates, and appends new facts; no row is ever updated
   v0 balance=0 -> appended {"type":"AccountOpened","owner":"alice"}
   v1 balance=0 -> appended {"type":"MoneyDeposited","amount":100}
   v2 balance=100 -> appended {"type":"MoneyWithdrawn","amount":30}

## 2. Invariants are checked against rebuilt state
   concept: withdraw 500 with balance 70 must be rejected, and nothing is appended
   rejected: insufficient funds: balance 70, asked 500
   check ok: withdrawing 500 from a balance of 70 is rejected and appends nothing

## 3. Optimistic concurrency
   concept: two writers read the same version; the first append wins, the second hits UNIQUE(stream_id, version)
   writer A and writer B both read v3
   writer A appended v4
   writer B: ConcurrencyError=true (stream account-699a5293-da4f-47cf-be5b-bcf10a5765f4 moved past v3)
   check ok: the second writer with the same expected version gets a ConcurrencyError

## 3b. Retry
   concept: two concurrent withdrawals of 60 from 71: the loser reloads, re-decides against the new balance, and is rejected instead of overdrawing
   v4 balance=71 -> appended {"type":"MoneyWithdrawn","amount":60}
   writer A: conflict on attempt 1 (stream account-699a5293-da4f-47cf-be5b-bcf10a5765f4 moved past v4), reloading and deciding again
   writer A rejected: insufficient funds: balance 11, asked 60
   check ok: of two concurrent withdrawals of 60 from 71, one wins and the retried loser is rejected for insufficient funds

## 4. The stream is the source of truth
   concept: the full history is stored; current state is only a left fold over it
┌─────────┬───┬──────────────────┬─────────┬────────┐
│ (index) │ v │ type             │ owner   │ amount │
├─────────┼───┼──────────────────┼─────────┼────────┤
│ 0       │ 1 │ 'AccountOpened'  │ 'alice' │        │
│ 1       │ 2 │ 'MoneyDeposited' │         │ 100    │
│ 2       │ 3 │ 'MoneyWithdrawn' │         │ 30     │
│ 3       │ 4 │ 'MoneyDeposited' │         │ 1      │
│ 4       │ 5 │ 'MoneyWithdrawn' │         │ 60     │
└─────────┴───┴──────────────────┴─────────┴────────┘
   current state: { owner: 'alice', balance: 11, version: 5 }
   check ok: the stream holds exactly 5 facts, versions 1 to 5, and folds to balance 11
   check ok: nothing from a rejected command or a losing writer was stored

## 5. Time travel
   concept: replay only the events recorded before a date to answer "what was the state at the end of March?"
   as of 2026-10-04T00:48:51.479Z: { owner: 'alice', balance: 70, version: 3 }
   check ok: replaying the events recorded before v4 gives the state at v3, balance 70
   by version is the same fold over a prefix, e.g. as of v1: { owner: 'alice', balance: 0, version: 1 }

## 6. Projections (read models)
   concept: any new view can be derived later by replaying the same events, e.g. total deposited
   total deposited = 101
   check ok: a projection added later derives total deposited = 101 from the same events

